              "source_id": "alcf-status",
              "name": "ALCF computing status",
              "why_not_read": "Blocked probe. The status page is an Angular application and its data paths return HTTP 403 with a Cloudflare challenge to a scripted client, which under decision 0007 is blocked_probe and NOT gated: a WAF refusing this client shape says nothing about whether the data is public. One real-browser check, watching the application's own network calls, would settle both the endpoint and the posture. Joins the blocked-probe backlog. Note, 2026-10-20. One plain GET of the status page answered 200 with the application shell, so the 403 did not recur; one probe from one machine is not evidence that the posture changed. The page's own data path was found and is not a candidate: it is undocumented and carries queued and running job records, which this project does not read for any facility. ALCF documents a separate machine route, its implementation of the IRI Facility API at api.alcf.anl.gov, whose status reads answered a plain GET with JSON. Under decision 0025 that is a different source with its own terms, and it waits on a terms review before it is registered; this manifest stays proposed until then."
